?SECTION NEW
# zone:interface:address scopes a rule to one interface AND one address, the
# documented three-part SOURCE form (shorewall-rules(5)). SSH is allowed only
# from 10.0.2.2 arriving on WAN (eth0); HTTP only from 10.0.3.2 arriving on
# WAN2 (eth1). A packet on the right interface with the wrong source address
# must not match.
ACCEPT	net:WAN:10.0.2.2	$FW		tcp	22
ACCEPT	net:WAN2:10.0.3.2	$FW		tcp	80
